STATUS: Generate one transparent two-icon sprite sheet for the completed and
locked campaign-level plaque states. Base both badges on the newest campaign
map screenshot; Android will place them at the right side of the matching
number plaque.

## Reference input

- Attach the campaign-map screenshot showing the completed level 1 checkmark
  and the locked-level padlocks. Use those small status badges as the primary
  reference.
- Attach the extracted completed and locked level-plaque assets as secondary
  references for matching their gold, dark-metal, and parchment materials.
- Keep each badge separate from its level plaque. Do not copy the map,
  fortress/boss artwork, level number, or progress UI.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG sprite sheet:
  `campaign_level_status_icons_sheet.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/campaign/ui/`.
- Canvas: 2:1 landscape, RGBA. Prefer 1024 x 512 pixels. If the image
  generator uses a different fixed resolution, preserve the 2:1 aspect and
  two evenly spaced states.
- Arrange two equal-width cells horizontally, in this order:
  1. completed check badge;
  2. locked padlock badge.
- Center one badge in each cell. Keep their visible bounds close in size so
  both appear balanced when rendered at 16 dp.
- Use genuine transparent alpha around each badge. Do not draw a checkerboard
  or a continuous background behind the cells.
- Export one sprite sheet only; the two cells will be extracted into separate
  runtime assets after review.

## Badge design

- **Completed, first cell:** a compact, round deep-green enamel badge with a
  bold ivory checkmark. Add a restrained antique-gold rim so it fits the
  completed dark plaque without overpowering the level number.
- **Locked, second cell:** a compact, dark-brown iron badge with a clear
  antique-gold padlock. Match the small rectangular padlock treatment shown
  beside locked level numbers in the screenshot.
- Give both badges the same apparent visual weight, detail level, edge
  quality, and warm Orc-fantasy materials. Their silhouettes may differ to
  preserve the round check and rectangular lock treatments.
- Keep each mark bold and simple enough to read at 16 dp. Avoid tiny rivets,
  thin shackle lines, or delicate highlights that disappear at phone size.
- Keep light, shadow, and metallic highlights attached to the badge. Do not
  add a glow or aura around either state.

## Separation from live UI

- Generate the complete small badge only. Do not include a level plaque,
  number, text, label, fortress, boss, map, terrain, or other UI.
- Do not draw a second outline or a larger circle/medallion around either
  badge. The completed circle and compact locked tile are the badges
  themselves.
- The level number remains a separate text overlay. Available levels have no
  status icon and must not receive a third sprite-sheet cell.
- Keep both cells otherwise transparent and their contents fully inside each
  cell.

## Extraction after review

- Split the sheet into two equal-width columns using its actual dimensions,
  preserving the left-to-right order; do not assume fixed pixel boundaries
  if the generator changes resolution.
- Trim transparent margins around each badge and normalize both crops to the
  same pixel dimensions while preserving alpha.
- The extracted source assets will be named:
  `campaign_level_status_completed.png` and
  `campaign_level_status_locked.png`.
- Preview both at 16 dp beside the level plaques before importing them into
  Android drawable resources.

## Negative prompt

opaque background, checkerboard, continuous background, sprite sheet with
extra cells, third available icon, level plaque, number, text, letters,
labels, fortress, boss, map, terrain, status ring, aura, glow, large
medallion, shield, pin, oversized ornament, completed lock, locked checkmark,
thin checkmark, tiny lock, unreadable detail, modern flat icon, polished
plastic, jagged alpha, colored fringe, detached shadow, watermark, signature

## Review checklist

- Confirm one transparent 2:1 sprite sheet contains exactly two centered
  badges in the stated order.
- Confirm the completed badge is green with an ivory checkmark and the locked
  badge is dark metal with a gold padlock.
- Confirm both have genuine transparent backgrounds and clean alpha edges.
- Preview at 16 dp and verify the check and lock remain immediately
  recognizable.
- Confirm no plaque, number, text, map, fortress, boss, or third state is
  included.
